 "notes": "Dark photon kinetic-mixing limit from Jupiter's magnetic field (Juno MAG data), the paper's headline plotted result. Traced the red 'Juno MAG (This Work)' 95% credible curve from Fig. 7 (e-print plots/limitJeff.png), a raster PNG, by pixel analysis: log-log axis calibrated on decade ticks (x: 10^-17 eV at px921, 775 px/decade; y: eps=1 at px399, 708 px/decade), legend box masked. epsilon = chi is reported directly (paper's variable is the kinetic mixing epsilon). U-shaped curve; excluded region is above/inside the curve. Minimum bound eps<=2.8e-3 at m_X=2.0e-15 eV (text), consistent with trace (~2.86e-3 near 1.6-1.9e-15 eV). Endpoints anchored to text: at eps=1, m_X<=3.2e-18 eV (left) and m_X>=3.2e-14 eV (right). Limit is explicitly independent of dark photon relic density, so dm_density_assumed=null. Paper also gives a photon-mass bound m_gamma<2.5e-18 eV (Eq. 5.5); the dark photon plane is the main plottable result. The COBE/FIRAS, Pioneer 10 and Juno-dipole curves in Fig.7 are external references, not this work.",
